Description: Dispatch the seat state queued for a test device before the device helpers return.
 The input thread queues the touch mode resulting from adding or removing a device with an idle source of
 G_PRIORITY_HIGH before it queues the device event, which the backend's event source of G_PRIORITY_DEFAULT dispatches.
 GLib releases its lock while it checks a source, so the idle source can be attached after the sources of higher
 priority were checked in an iteration whose check of the backend's event source then finds the event. Clutter
 processes a DEVICE_REMOVED event at once, so meta_backend_test_remove_test_device() returned at the "device-removed"
 signal with the previous touch mode, and the test monitor-orientation-tests failed with
 "'clutter_seat_get_touch_mode (seat)' should be FALSE" in a CI build of this repository (job 18411200840) and in
 mutter's own CI (job 7387372). Clutter queues a DEVICE_ADDED event on the stage for a later iteration, so adding a
 device is not affected.
 .
 The helpers which add and remove a test device now also dispatch the sources ready after the device signal, which
 include the idle source, as it is attached before the device event is queued.
 .
 With the test's main loop instrumented to sleep 1 ms in the check of a source between the two priorities, the test
 failed in 98 of 100 runs without the change and in 0 of 100 with it. Without the instrumentation, the test passed
 500 of 500 runs with the change. It changes only the tests.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-27
--- a/src/tests/meta-backend-test.c
+++ b/src/tests/meta-backend-test.c
@@ -86,6 +86,19 @@ set_true_cb (gboolean *value)
   *value = TRUE;
 }
 
+static void
+dispatch_queued_seat_state (void)
+{
+  /* The input thread queues the seat state resulting from adding or removing
+   * a device, like touch mode, with an idle source of higher priority before
+   * the device event, but GLib can still dispatch the device event first when
+   * the idle source was attached while GLib was checking the sources of an
+   * iteration. The idle source is already attached when the device signal is
+   * emitted, so it is dispatched here.
+   */
+  while (g_main_context_iteration (NULL, FALSE));
+}
+
 ClutterVirtualInputDevice *
 meta_backend_test_add_test_device (MetaBackendTest        *backend_test,
                                    ClutterInputDeviceType  device_type,
@@ -105,6 +118,8 @@ meta_backend_test_add_test_device (MetaB
   while (!was_updated)
     g_main_context_iteration (NULL, TRUE);
 
+  dispatch_queued_seat_state ();
+
   g_signal_handlers_disconnect_by_func (seat, set_true_cb, &was_updated);
 
   return virtual_device;
@@ -127,6 +142,8 @@ meta_backend_test_remove_test_device (Me
   while (!was_updated)
     g_main_context_iteration (NULL, TRUE);
 
+  dispatch_queued_seat_state ();
+
   g_signal_handlers_disconnect_by_func (seat, set_true_cb, &was_updated);
 }
 
